Rule Category	Rule Name	Purpose	Metric	Warning Threshold	Critical Threshold	Evaluation Window	Check Interval	Consecutive Runs (Warning)	Consecutive Runs (Critical)	Severity	Action	How it Works		
Synthetics	Application Availability	Detect application outages using synthetic monitors.	summary.up / Monitor Status	2 consecutive failures or Availability <99%	3 consecutive failures or Availability <95%	10 min (15 min for availability %)	1 min	2	3	Warning/Critical	Notify support / Create incident	Rule evaluates every minute. If monitor continues failing for 2 (warning) or 3 (critical) consecutive evaluations within the lookback window, the alert is triggered.		
CPU	CPU Utilisation	Detect sustained high CPU utilisation.	system.cpu.total.norm.pct	>75%	>90%	10 min	1 min	2	3	Warning/Critical	Notify support / Create incident	Every minute Kibana evaluates the previous 10 minutes of CPU metrics. If CPU remains above threshold for the configured consecutive runs, the alert is triggered.		
Memory	Memory Utilisation	Detect sustained high memory usage.	system.memory.actual.used.pct	>80%	>90%	10 min	1 min	2	3	Warning/Critical	Notify support / Create incident	Every minute Kibana evaluates the previous 10 minutes of memory metrics. If memory remains above threshold for the configured consecutive runs, the alert is triggered.		
Filesystem	Filesystem Usage	Detect critical disk utilisation before the application or operating system runs out of disk space.	system.filesystem.used.pct	>80%	>90%	10 min	1 min	2	3	Warning/Critical	Notify support / Create incident	Every minute Kibana evaluates filesystem usage over the previous 10 minutes. If disk usage exceeds the threshold for 2 (warning) or 3 (critical) consecutive evaluations, the alert is triggered. When usage drops below the threshold, the alert recovers.		
														
